1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 6)

3
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,920
You guys are here.

4
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,120
Say hello to him.

5
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,199
Hello, Milan.

6
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,480
Hey there!

7
00:01:18,159 --> 00:01:19,239
You're here too.

8
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:21,079
Yeah.

9
00:01:22,599 --> 00:01:23,799
I'm here to protect these two.

10
00:01:25,439 --> 00:01:26,359
Are you guys happy today?

11
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,400
Yeah.

12
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,599
It's really crowded today.

13
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,798
Stay close to us.

14
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:30,239
Okay?

15
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:31,439
Okay.

16
00:01:31,879 --> 00:01:32,879
Good kids.

17
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:33,599
Yeah.

18
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,559
Didn't someone say he'd come with us?

19
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,560
Where is he?

20
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,256
I knew we couldn't count
on him when it matters.

21
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,440
Master P'Eng had some
urgent business to take care of.

22
00:01:40,519 --> 00:01:42,239
So he might be a little late.

23
00:01:42,959 --> 00:01:44,079
Can't count on who for what?

24
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:47,760
Nothing.

25
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:48,959
Boss P'Eng is here.

26
00:01:50,599 --> 00:01:51,640
You heard wrong.

27
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,055
It's because we can count on you

28
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:55,839
that they got to come
to the amusement park.

29
00:01:56,817 --> 00:01:58,055
Hi, P'Eng.

30
00:01:58,079 --> 00:01:59,079
Hey.

31
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:00,279
Thank you, P'Eng.

32
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:00,799
Don't mention it.

33
00:02:00,959 --> 00:02:02,040
Such a show-off.

34
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,560
Only knows how to win over kids.

35
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,040
Hey.

36
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:07,519
This is a paradise for kids.

37
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,280
Of course you want to make them happy.

38
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:11,640
Why don't you give it a try?

39
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,080
I could never act like him.

40
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:16,599
A Pong.

41
00:02:17,159 --> 00:02:18,159
Don't worry.

42
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,560
He's genuinely trying to make
things right with everyone.

43
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:24,599
Mr. Milan.

44
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,599
It's almost time.

45
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,496
The crew says you can get
changed whenever you're ready.

46
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:27,960
Okay.

47
00:02:28,159 --> 00:02:29,359
Tell them I'll be right there.

48
00:02:29,919 --> 00:02:30,680
So, Pao Bei,

49
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:31,439
and Boss P'Eng.

50
00:02:31,961 --> 00:02:33,575
Why don't you take Xiaotong
and Xiaoya to go play first?

51
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:34,800
We'll meet up once I'm done.

52
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:35,560
Yeah.

53
00:02:35,719 --> 00:02:36,719
Sounds good.

54
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,119
I'll leave Mingkun here with you.

55
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,560
Okay.

56
00:02:38,879 --> 00:02:39,960
Hey, what about me?

57
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,439
Come with us!

58
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,520
No way.

59
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,360
Then stick with me.

60
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,479
Don't forget our deal.

61
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,855
These are my leftover lottery tickets.

62
00:02:49,879 --> 00:02:51,319
If there's a winning ticket in here,

63
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,680
I'll be your assistant.

64
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:54,159
What do you say?

65
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:55,319
Care to make a bet?

66
00:02:57,039 --> 00:02:57,400
Bring it on.

67
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:57,800
Did you just hit me?

68
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,800
All right.

69
00:02:58,919 --> 00:02:59,439
Off you go.

70
00:02:59,759 --> 00:03:00,280
Let's go.

71
00:03:00,759 --> 00:03:01,280
Go have fun.

72
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,319
Yeah.

73
00:03:02,479 --> 00:03:03,479
Let's go.

74
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,080
See you guys later.

75
00:03:30,319 --> 00:03:32,400
Look, this fish has
stripes just like a zebra.

76
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,919
The color is so pretty.

77
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:49,199
Come here, Xiaoya.

78
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,920
I'll show you how to feed the sea turtles.

79
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,560
Come here.

80
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,560
Take a little break.

81
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,840
Are you having fun today?

82
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:04,800
You must be thirsty.

83
00:04:05,039 --> 00:04:06,039
Have some water.

84
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,080
Thank you, P'Eng.

85
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,639
Do you like the jellyfish
or Mr. Turtle better?

86
00:04:12,759 --> 00:04:13,840
I like them both!

87
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:19,279
Slow down, Xiaoya.

88
00:04:23,759 --> 00:04:25,000
So many bubbles!

89
00:04:25,639 --> 00:04:27,199
The merry-go-round!

90
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,960
Are you scared of the pirate ship?

91
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:54,480
Of course not!

92
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,120
I'm too scared to look!

93
00:05:08,079 --> 00:05:09,639
It feels like we're flying!

94
00:05:37,279 --> 00:05:38,480
Be careful, everyone.

95
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,559
We can take photos together,

96
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,055
but please line up in an orderly fashion.

97
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:42,720
Can we take a picture?

98
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,720
Is that okay?

99
00:05:43,759 --> 00:05:44,958
Alright alright alright.

100
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:45,839
Here, hand it to me.

101
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:46,920
One by one.

102
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,359
Thank you.

103
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,199
Smile!

104
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,199
Say cheese!

105
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,759
Come on.

106
00:05:59,839 --> 00:06:01,055
Let's do one more from another angle.

107
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:02,160
Look happy!

108
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,839
Thank you.

109
00:06:16,639 --> 00:06:17,639
Keep it up!

110
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:18,759
Thanks.

111
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,638
Big smile!

112
00:06:20,639 --> 00:06:22,318
Milan!

113
00:06:22,319 --> 00:06:24,120
You set the stage on fire!

114
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:28,759
Watch your step.

115
00:06:28,759 --> 00:06:29,519
Please keep your distance.

116
00:06:29,519 --> 00:06:30,439
Everyone, please be careful.

117
00:06:30,439 --> 00:06:31,160
Be careful.

118
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,160
Keep your distance.

119
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,680
At your three o'clock.

120
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,800
Follow me.

121
00:06:34,839 --> 00:06:35,959
Be careful and stay close.

122
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,639
Watch your step.

123
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:40,199
Coming through!

124
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:44,679
Hello, everyone!

125
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,919
Right behind me is the most
popular attraction in Tailan,

126
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,800
the Giant Pendulum!

127
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,559
Now, since I'm afraid of heights,

128
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:53,318
I'm going to pass on riding it today.

129
00:06:53,319 --> 00:06:55,920
If this video hits a million likes,

130
00:06:56,079 --> 00:06:57,119
then next time,

131
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:59,959
I'll make a video taking
on the Giant Pendulum!

132
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,079
How is it?

133
00:07:01,199 --> 00:07:02,079
Does it look good here?

134
00:07:02,199 --> 00:07:03,199
It's fine.

135
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:04,599
After showing you guys around so much,

136
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,399
I'm getting thirsty

137
00:07:05,399 --> 00:07:06,079
and pretty tired.

138
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:08,360
So now I'm going to go grab a bite to eat.

139
00:07:08,839 --> 00:07:10,519
This is my assistant, A Pong.

140
00:07:12,199 --> 00:07:13,199
And so...

141
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,399
Watch out!

142
00:07:14,399 --> 00:07:15,399
I'm so sorry.

143
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:17,199
Are you okay?

144
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,279
I'm fine.

145
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,240
Really?

146
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:24,319
It's nothing.

147
00:07:25,639 --> 00:07:26,639
Mr. Milan.

148
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:27,879
The lounge is over that way.

149
00:07:27,879 --> 00:07:28,639
Please follow me.

150
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,439
Okay.

151
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,680
Let's go.

152
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:34,480
Mr. Milan.

153
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:38,079
Do you need us to send more security?

154
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,360
Not for now.

155
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,439
He handled it really well.

156
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,680
Could I get a quick touch-up on my makeup?

157
00:07:50,736 --> 00:07:52,096
We just need to shoot one
section of footage and we're good.

158
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,120
Got it.

159
00:07:56,399 --> 00:07:57,600
Take a few more shots for me.

160
00:07:58,399 --> 00:07:59,719
What else am I supposed to shoot?

161
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,240
Just shoot it however you want.

162
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,079
Aw, so cute!

163
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:04,759
Fine.

164
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:07,720
Hey.

165
00:08:08,319 --> 00:08:09,120
Oh, it's you.

166
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:09,720
Yeah.

167
00:08:10,079 --> 00:08:11,119
How did my shots turn out?

168
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:11,959
They're...

169
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:13,240
They're not bad.

170
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:15,398
Looking sharp!

171
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:16,199
Did you get it?

172
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:16,920
Does it look good?

173
00:08:17,199 --> 00:08:18,000
It looks great.

174
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:18,639
Take a look.

175
00:08:18,839 --> 00:08:19,839
See?

176
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,839
Aren't you leaving yet?

177
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,639
A huge crowd is heading this way soon.

178
00:08:27,759 --> 00:08:29,039
If you don't leave now,
you won't be able to get out.

179
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,120
Just giving you a heads-up.

180
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,680
It's fine.

181
00:08:32,279 --> 00:08:33,519
I've got someone protecting me.

182
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,879
You actually know him?

183
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,398
When he told me last time,

184
00:08:37,399 --> 00:08:38,679
I thought he was kidding.

185
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,918
You even know my fans.

186
00:08:40,919 --> 00:08:41,919
Yeah.

187
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,240
You're pretty well-connected.

188
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,080
I told you.

189
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,615
She's the one who asked me
to deliver those flowers last time.

190
00:08:47,639 --> 00:08:48,719
See? I wasn't lying to you.

191
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,200
That was me.

192
00:08:52,639 --> 00:08:53,816
Looks like people are
coming from over there.

193
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,000
Shouldn't you guys get going?

194
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,440
Hold them back for a second.

195
00:08:56,441 --> 00:08:57,521
I'll be fine with just him.

196
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,320
Milan!

197
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,320
Bye!

198
00:09:01,279 --> 00:09:02,279
Stay back!

199
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,080
You can't go through!

200
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:03,799
Everyone, please calm down!

201
00:09:03,799 --> 00:09:04,799
Please stay back!

202
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,960
Don't go over there.

203
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,120
Milan!

204
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:18,919
I think we shook them off.

205
00:09:21,799 --> 00:09:23,159
Aren't you an athlete?

206
00:09:23,279 --> 00:09:25,359
Why are you so out of
breath after just a short run?

207
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,200
Come on, man.

208
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,759
Do you know how many years ago that was?

209
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:30,679
Besides,

210
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,919
this bag of yours weighs a ton.

211
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,080
Why don't you try carrying it yourself?

212
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:37,319
You look pretty strong, so I figured

213
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,535
this little bit of weight
was nothing to you.

214
00:09:38,559 --> 00:09:39,159
Give it to me.

215
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,200
I'll carry it myself.

216
00:09:42,919 --> 00:09:44,199
Didn't you say it's super heavy?

217
00:09:44,559 --> 00:09:46,079
I can't have you wearing yourself out.

218
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,839
You're not my assistant.

219
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,480
You're my old...

220
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,960
classmate, after all.

221
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,320
Right?

222
00:09:53,799 --> 00:09:55,000
Alright, cut the crap.

223
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:55,799
What do you want to ride?

224
00:09:55,799 --> 00:09:56,799
Hurry up.

225
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,840
Don't waste time.

226
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,200
What do you want to do?

227
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,360
I'll go with you.

228
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,495
If anything, I should be going
along with what you want.

229
00:10:05,519 --> 00:10:07,239
I'm only here thanks to you.

230
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:07,879
No,

231
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,320
it's not thanks to me.

232
00:10:09,799 --> 00:10:12,278
It's thanks to Boss
P'Eng, the guy you hate.

233
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:14,079
I'm not the one who
got you guys these spots.

234
00:10:16,879 --> 00:10:17,360
How about this?

235
00:10:17,679 --> 00:10:18,679
Rock, paper, scissors.

236
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:19,960
Winner decides.

237
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:20,960
No.

238
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,080
Let's say it together.

239
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,159
What if we want to go on the same ride?

240
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,879
No way.

241
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,120
Why not?

242
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:28,879
Did you forget?

243
00:10:29,159 --> 00:10:30,279
Back when we were in school,

244
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:32,719
we used to get the exact
same test scores all the time.

245
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:36,879
That's just because both of
our grades were equally terrible.

246
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:38,320
Come on, just say it.

247
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:38,960
I'll count down from three.

248
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:39,960
We'll say it together.

249
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:41,320
Three,

250
00:10:41,759 --> 00:10:42,240
two,

251
00:10:42,279 --> 00:10:42,759
one.

252
00:10:42,759 --> 00:10:43,759
- Roller coaster!

253
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,678
See?

254
00:10:52,679 --> 00:10:54,439
I told you we were on the same wavelength.

255
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,480
Totally in sync.

256
00:10:57,559 --> 00:10:59,000
Why are you so touchy-feely?

257
00:10:59,399 --> 00:11:01,959
Do you have any idea how
many fans would kill to hug me?

258
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,440
And here you are complaining.

259
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,879
I'm not one of your fans.

260
00:11:10,039 --> 00:11:11,039
Don't forget

261
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,359
who said back then

262
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,240
that he'd be my very
first fan once I debuted?

263
00:11:16,073 --> 00:11:17,073
Hmmm?

264
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:18,919
That...

265
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,120
That was so many years ago.

266
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,639
How do you still remember that?

267
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,000
Thanks for today.

268
00:11:35,759 --> 00:11:36,840
So, how was today?

269
00:11:37,879 --> 00:11:38,879
How was what?

270
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,399
I mean, how did I do today?

271
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,720
Did your brother

272
00:11:42,721 --> 00:11:45,480
have any feedback or anything?

273
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,159
Wait till they get back with the ice cream,

274
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,320
and ask him yourself.

275
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:00,639
That's really pretty.

276
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:01,799
And so tall.

277
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,440
I'd love to take a ride.

278
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:08,840
Look, I know I'm tall,

279
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:09,959
but calling me "pretty"...

280
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,200
isn't that going a bit too far?

281
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,960
I mean,

282
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:15,080
at least use "dashingly
handsome" to describe me.

283
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:16,639
And besides...

284
00:12:17,519 --> 00:12:18,519
Take...

285
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,840
take a ride?

286
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,878
I only took you guys out once,

287
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:24,480
and you're already throwing yourself at me?

288
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,639
Boss P'Eng,

289
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:31,080
I was talking about the
Ferris wheel right behind you.

290
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:37,800
I really want to go up there and
see what Mancheng looks like.

291
00:12:48,679 --> 00:12:49,480
Let me take Xiaoya.

292
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,000
P'Eng,

293
00:12:50,001 --> 00:12:51,081
carrying her is too tiring.

294
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:52,159
It's fine.

295
00:12:52,279 --> 00:12:53,000
She's not heavy.

296
00:12:53,001 --> 00:12:54,321
The kid's probably just worn out.

297
00:12:55,559 --> 00:12:57,559
Looks like the Ferris
wheel is closed for the day.

298
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,680
I just went over and asked.

299
00:12:58,919 --> 00:13:00,976
They have a minor issue and
need to do some maintenance.

300
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,720
We probably won't be able to ride it today.

301
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,600
What?

302
00:13:05,039 --> 00:13:06,558
It's fine every other day,

303
00:13:06,559 --> 00:13:08,519
why does it have to break
down today of all days?

304
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,855
What's so fun about that anyway?

305
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:11,495
I'll take you to see the
fireworks show later.

306
00:13:11,519 --> 00:13:12,440
P'Eng,

307
00:13:12,441 --> 00:13:13,879
what's a fireworks show?

308
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,440
How do I put it?

309
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,039
It's when they shoot fireworks

310
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,878
up into the sky, and it's super pretty.

311
00:13:22,879 --> 00:13:24,840
It goes "boom" like this,

312
00:13:25,879 --> 00:13:27,079
with tons of colors,

313
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,999
and it looks like stars
falling from the sky.

314
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Oh!

315
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,080
Okay.

316
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,255
Anyway, you'll see for yourself in a bit.

317
00:13:35,279 --> 00:13:35,720
Okay.

318
00:13:35,919 --> 00:13:38,038
Master, today's fireworks show...

319
00:13:38,039 --> 00:13:39,320
seems to be canceled too.

320
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,399
Aw, what a shame.

321
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,560
Why do I feel like the
universe is out to get me again?

322
00:13:58,159 --> 00:14:00,199
Maybe fate just doesn't
want to give me the chance.

323
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:01,840
Chance for what?

324
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,240
You know,

325
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,959
the chance to see the beautiful
night view of Mancheng.

326
00:14:06,919 --> 00:14:08,960
Maybe if I get a taste
of something good once,

327
00:14:09,279 --> 00:14:10,879
I'll just want to hold onto it forever.

328
00:14:11,519 --> 00:14:14,080
It's honestly better
to never have it at all.

329
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,240
It's fine this way.

330
00:14:20,919 --> 00:14:21,919
Come on, get up.

331
00:14:22,679 --> 00:14:23,879
I'm taking you guys somewhere.

332
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Where?

333
00:14:33,399 --> 00:14:34,159
Master,

334
00:14:34,399 --> 00:14:36,360
little Xiaoya looks completely exhausted.

335
00:14:36,759 --> 00:14:38,519
I'll take her back to
the car to rest first.

336
00:14:41,159 --> 00:14:42,159
Let's go.

337
00:15:52,759 --> 00:15:53,959
Milan!

338
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,840
Milan, can I get a picture with you?

339
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,240
It's Milan!

340
00:15:59,159 --> 00:16:00,279
Everyone, please be careful!

341
00:16:01,279 --> 00:16:02,759
Milan!

342
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:03,600
Excuse me.

343
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,320
Milan!

344
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,320
Don't go!

345
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,839
Jeez, where did you run off to?

346
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,759
I looked everywhere for you.

347
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,959
I figured I'd disappear for once

348
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:25,840
so you'd know how it feels.

349
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,999
Man, I was chased the whole way here.

350
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:28,519
Hurry, let's go.

351
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Come with me.

352
00:16:51,919 --> 00:16:53,039
It's gorgeous.

353
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,639
The night view here is amazing.

354
00:16:55,519 --> 00:16:56,519
I wanna see too!

355
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,039
Bro, give me a piggyback ride, quick!

356
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,680
What's wrong with you?

357
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,118
You look a little pale.

358
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:10,119
I...

359
00:17:11,799 --> 00:17:12,919
I'm a bit afraid of heights.

360
00:17:14,519 --> 00:17:15,599
Afraid of heights?

361
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,456
And you still dared
to ride the pirate ship?

362
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,000
Yeah.

363
00:17:18,319 --> 00:17:19,319
Now you know

364
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,559
how much I sacrificed.

365
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,960
Come here, I'll lift you up.

366
00:17:26,359 --> 00:17:28,680
P'Eng is a scaredy-cat
who's afraid of heights!

367
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:29,880
Hold on.

368
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,575
Acrophobia is a natural physical reaction. It
has nothing to do with being a scaredy-cat.

369
00:17:33,599 --> 00:17:34,599
I am not a coward.

370
00:17:34,799 --> 00:17:35,799
Come here.

371
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:36,960
Get on my back.

372
00:17:37,319 --> 00:17:38,319
You'll be even higher up.

373
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,480
Okay!

374
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,839
One, two, three.

375
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:43,759
Are you sure you're okay?

376
00:17:44,039 --> 00:17:45,240
Don't drop my brother.

377
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,440
Don't underestimate me.

378
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,440
There we go.

379
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,119
The night view is so pretty, bro!

380
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:04,798
It's really gorgeous!

381
00:18:04,799 --> 00:18:06,278
P'Eng,

382
00:18:06,279 --> 00:18:07,959
maybe you should put me down.

383
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:08,960
Okay.

384
00:18:12,599 --> 00:18:14,399
I'll go get Mingkun and Xiaoya

385
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,760
so we can watch the view together.

386
00:18:15,799 --> 00:18:16,799
Okay.

387
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:17,920
Yeah.

388
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:24,559
Um...

389
00:18:24,799 --> 00:18:26,000
Why is your face so red?

390
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,080
Why don't we go rest over there for a bit?

391
00:18:28,559 --> 00:18:29,559
Sure.

392
00:18:37,279 --> 00:18:38,480
I'm feeling a bit better now.

393
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,880
I think I'm getting used to it.

394
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,759
It's so beautiful here.

395
00:18:49,359 --> 00:18:51,079
It's my first time seeing a view like this.

396
00:18:55,359 --> 00:18:56,959
So it's because you're afraid of heights

397
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,358
that you were so nervous
on the pirate ship, right?

398
00:18:59,359 --> 00:19:00,000
Yeah.

399
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,000
What did you think?

400
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,920
Fear of heights is a biological response.

401
00:19:03,039 --> 00:19:04,480
You can't control it, you know?

402
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,798
And here I thought our Boss P'Eng

403
00:19:10,799 --> 00:19:12,440
was completely fearless.

404
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,040
Turns out you're scared of something too.

405
00:19:17,559 --> 00:19:19,519
I think you're the one
who's completely fearless.

406
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,278
Actually, there are plenty of things

407
00:19:25,279 --> 00:19:26,799
that scare me too.

408
00:19:28,119 --> 00:19:29,200
Like what?

409
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:40,440
Like...

410
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,800
My biggest fear is running out of money.

411
00:19:43,119 --> 00:19:44,416
What's so scary about having no money?

412
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,440
Just make more.

413
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:46,720
You're perfectly capable.

414
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,200
A rich boy like you wouldn't understand.

415
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,480
Still, today,

416
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:56,240
thank you for making Xiaotong
and Xiaoya's wish come true.

417
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,480
Thank you from the bottom of my heart.

418
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:15,799
Their wish came true.

419
00:20:17,279 --> 00:20:18,279
What about yours?

420
00:20:19,359 --> 00:20:20,440
What's your wish?

421
00:20:35,759 --> 00:20:37,200
Xiaotong and Xiaoya...

422
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,559
Their wish

423
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:44,599
is my wish.

424
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:57,880
Hello?

425
00:20:58,559 --> 00:20:59,559
Yeah.

426
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:00,680
You can start now.

427
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,920
Am I keeping you from your work?

428
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,440
Should we head back?

429
00:21:05,759 --> 00:21:06,759
It's fine.

430
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,440
Tell me what your wish is first.

431
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:12,960
My wish?

432
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
What do you mean?

433
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,880
Before my mom passed
away, she used to say

434
00:21:19,039 --> 00:21:20,359
that when fireworks are blooming,

435
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:21,839
the wishes you make

436
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:24,240
are the most likely to come true.

437
00:21:26,079 --> 00:21:27,119
Really?

438
00:21:27,359 --> 00:21:29,200
That's the first time I've heard of that.

439
00:21:29,359 --> 00:21:30,079
It's true.

440
00:21:30,359 --> 00:21:32,359
All the wishes I made
before ended up coming true.

441
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:44,480
But there aren't any fireworks right now.

442
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:47,960
Close your eyes.

443
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,240
Huh?

444
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,480
Just close your eyes.

445
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Three,

446
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,480
two,

447
00:22:05,319 --> 00:22:05,839
one.

448
00:22:06,319 --> 00:22:07,319
Open them.

449
00:22:12,759 --> 00:22:14,240
Quick, make a wish now!

450
00:22:15,799 --> 00:22:18,279
I wish for Xiaotong and Xiaoya
to always be healthy and happy.

451
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:21,000
I wish for Mom to come back soon,

452
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:23,079
so we can live a peaceful, stable life.

453
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,240
And I wish...

454
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,119
Wait, how many wishes do I get?

455
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,200
Can I have three?

456
00:22:35,759 --> 00:22:37,160
Hey, I'm talking to you!

457
00:22:38,319 --> 00:22:39,480
Did you hear me?

458
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:42,359
Where did you go?

459
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,720
Here you go, Boss P'Eng.

460
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,160
Thanks.

461
00:24:17,079 --> 00:24:18,239
Looks pretty good.

462
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,279
Yeah.

463
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:24,879
I heard you guys got mobbed by fans today.

464
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:25,880
Are you okay?

465
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:28,680
Thankfully, A Pong was there.

466
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:31,200
Otherwise, I might've
really been trapped in there.

467
00:24:31,599 --> 00:24:33,319
He's the person you were looking for?

468
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:36,118
You two were really college classmates?

469
00:24:36,119 --> 00:24:37,119
Yeah.

470
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,160
We even sat next to each other.

471
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:40,760
What a coincidence, right?

472
00:24:42,119 --> 00:24:44,599
Though we really owe this
reunion to you, Boss P'Eng.

473
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,840
Otherwise, it might've taken
us forever to cross paths again.

474
00:24:55,799 --> 00:24:58,960
Who knows if that's a blessing or a curse.

475
00:24:59,839 --> 00:25:02,599
Every twist of fate is a blessing.

476
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:04,439
There's no such thing as a curse.

477
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:08,000
After all, isn't that how
you and Pao Bei met?

478
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,279
P'Eng.

479
00:25:19,279 --> 00:25:19,759
Yeah?

480
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,558
Can I trade this rose
for a bottle of water?

481
00:25:21,559 --> 00:25:23,078
My sister says she's a little thirsty.

482
00:25:23,079 --> 00:25:24,838
Of course you can.

483
00:25:24,839 --> 00:25:25,839
Here.

484
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,519
Some water,

485
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,319
and two barbecue skewers.

486
00:25:31,079 --> 00:25:32,079
Enjoy.

487
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:33,599
Thank you, P'Eng!

488
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,640
Off you go.

489
00:25:35,799 --> 00:25:37,519
Looks like you guys had a great time today.

490
00:25:40,759 --> 00:25:41,759
By the way,

491
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:45,360
about finding me an assistant
like you mentioned last time...

492
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:47,118
What do you think of A Pong?

493
00:25:47,119 --> 00:25:48,920
If you want to hire him, go ahead.

494
00:25:49,839 --> 00:25:51,720
Though I should warn you,

495
00:25:52,799 --> 00:25:53,799
with that temper of his,

496
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:55,760
isn't he a bit too much to handle?

497
00:25:59,319 --> 00:26:00,480
Well,

498
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,599
everything has its pros and cons.

499
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:04,696
Sometimes, when artists
like us play the good cop,

500
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:06,680
we need our assistants to play the bad cop.

501
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:07,920
Hmm.

502
00:26:08,680 --> 00:26:09,480
That's true.

503
00:26:09,599 --> 00:26:10,599
You're too nice.

504
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,136
People can easily walk all over you.

505
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:13,480
Having someone to back you up

506
00:26:14,119 --> 00:26:15,119
is actually a good thing.

507
00:26:16,839 --> 00:26:19,240
Actually, A Pong doesn't
really have a bad temper.

508
00:26:20,279 --> 00:26:21,798
He probably just cares
too much about his friends.

509
00:26:21,799 --> 00:26:24,960
So, Boss P'Eng,

510
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:26,720
please don't hold it against him.

511
00:26:27,759 --> 00:26:29,119
Me?

512
00:26:29,759 --> 00:26:31,000
I don't mind.

513
00:26:31,799 --> 00:26:34,839
Honestly, I actually
envy Pao Bei sometimes,

514
00:26:35,119 --> 00:26:37,480
having a buddy who'd risk his life for him.

515
00:26:37,839 --> 00:26:39,039
Someone like me

516
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,518
doesn't really have any friends.

517
00:26:42,519 --> 00:26:44,839
How can anyone go
through life without friends?

518
00:26:45,039 --> 00:26:46,119
Because when I was a kid,

519
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:49,558
my father only cared
about me studying hard,

520
00:26:49,559 --> 00:26:51,639
saying the company would
depend on me in the future.

521
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,840
He even controlled who
I could be friends with.

522
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:55,279
Besides,

523
00:26:57,599 --> 00:26:59,160
I don't like making friends anyway.

524
00:26:59,599 --> 00:27:01,440
Even though we're business partners,

525
00:27:01,559 --> 00:27:03,319
if you ever need a friend,

526
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,880
we can be your friends.

527
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:10,318
Honestly, once you get to know A Pong,

528
00:27:10,319 --> 00:27:12,119
you'll see he's a pretty
straightforward guy.

529
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:17,519
I can tell.

530
00:27:18,079 --> 00:27:20,519
Compared to those slick corporate types,

531
00:27:21,119 --> 00:27:24,598
I'd probably much rather hang out with him.

532
00:27:24,599 --> 00:27:25,640
You're right.

533
00:27:26,599 --> 00:27:28,559
That's why I've been wanting to hire him.

534
00:27:29,279 --> 00:27:31,920
And it just so happens he
got fired from his chef job.

535
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:34,320
It seems to have something to do with you.

536
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:35,919
As for that,

537
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,199
I'll get to the bottom of it.

538
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,200
Alright.

539
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:39,920
Then about this job,

540
00:27:40,119 --> 00:27:41,399
I'll ask him what he thinks, too.

541
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:42,400
Okay.

542
00:27:42,440 --> 00:27:44,199
Still, having your approval

543
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,519
makes me really happy.

544
00:27:46,599 --> 00:27:47,640
Come on.

545
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,039
Cheers to you.

546
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:00,640
Master P'Eng,

547
00:28:00,839 --> 00:28:03,480
Mr. Pao Bei and Mr. A Pong
have finished preparing dinner.

548
00:28:03,799 --> 00:28:04,720
Should we serve it now?

549
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:05,720
Go ahead.

550
00:28:59,759 --> 00:29:00,759
Let's dance together.

551
00:29:07,039 --> 00:29:08,079
I'm so full.

552
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:10,535
It's all your fault for
making the food so delicious.

553
00:29:10,559 --> 00:29:12,599
I'm going to have to starve
myself again tomorrow.

554
00:29:14,599 --> 00:29:15,240
Don't mention it.

555
00:29:15,241 --> 00:29:16,521
I'm just glad you guys liked it.

556
00:29:17,519 --> 00:29:19,118
We wanted to thank
you for hosting us anyway,

557
00:29:19,119 --> 00:29:20,639
after showing us around all day today.

558
00:29:20,839 --> 00:29:22,999
You've thanked them
a million times already.

559
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,240
Stop making them thank us back.

560
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:29,240
Hey, take it easy on the drinks.

561
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,000
Don't drink too much.

562
00:29:32,519 --> 00:29:33,640
So what if I do?

563
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,479
This place of yours is so nice.

564
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:36,520
I'm crashing here tonight.

565
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:39,118
Look, there's booze and flowers here.

566
00:29:39,119 --> 00:29:40,599
It's way better than my place.

567
00:29:42,119 --> 00:29:43,119
It's fine.

568
00:29:43,599 --> 00:29:44,856
He can hold his liquor pretty well.

569
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,280
I've never even seen him get drunk.

570
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,200
It's fine.

571
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:50,319
If he gets drunk later,

572
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:51,479
I'll get a room ready for him.

573
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:52,079
Don't worry.

574
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,639
Hey, Big Devil!

575
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,640
Oh, no, wait.

576
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:56,200
Our Boss P'Eng!

577
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,839
Don't just drink by yourself.

578
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:01,278
When it comes to alcohol,

579
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:04,119
it's only fun when
everyone drinks together!

580
00:30:04,839 --> 00:30:07,119
Come on, cheers to you!

581
00:30:10,759 --> 00:30:11,759
Here!

582
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:18,319
Come on, Boss P'Eng.

583
00:30:18,839 --> 00:30:20,799
Here's a toast to you!

584
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:22,319
Why aren't you toasting me?

585
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:24,320
Do you look down on me or something?

586
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:26,160
Huh?

587
00:30:27,079 --> 00:30:28,079
You...

588
00:30:28,319 --> 00:30:29,839
Who are you?

589
00:30:30,519 --> 00:30:33,519
I only toast to our most
beloved Boss P'Eng!

590
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:36,079
Right, Boss P'Eng?

591
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:39,439
Boss P'Eng, I love you so much!

592
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:42,399
Just like a mouse loves cheese!

593
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,720
Okay.

594
00:30:44,079 --> 00:30:45,799
Drink up, Boss P'Eng!

595
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:47,240
Drink up!

596
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:53,839
Boss P'Eng, you're a real man!

597
00:30:54,039 --> 00:30:55,039
Downed it in one gulp!

598
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:56,200
What a guy!

599
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:57,839
I respect that!

600
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,440
What are you doing?

601
00:31:00,441 --> 00:31:01,519
I love you, man!

602
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:04,440
Boss P'Eng is so cool!

603
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:06,559
He chugged the whole thing!

604
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:11,559
Wait, why is Boss P'Eng blushing?

605
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:14,640
A Pong, you've really had too much.

606
00:31:14,799 --> 00:31:15,799
Stop drinking.

607
00:31:18,119 --> 00:31:18,680
Mingkun.

608
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:19,680
Look at him.

609
00:31:24,039 --> 00:31:24,559
Mingkun.

610
00:31:25,039 --> 00:31:26,775
Could you please get a
guest room ready for A Pong?

611
00:31:26,799 --> 00:31:28,399
Don't worry, it's already taken care of.

612
00:31:29,119 --> 00:31:29,759
Rest assured.

613
00:31:30,039 --> 00:31:31,399
I'll take him to his room to rest.

614
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:33,280
Your brother and sister are still here.

615
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:35,518
No need for that extra room.

616
00:31:35,519 --> 00:31:36,639
He can stay with me tonight.

617
00:31:37,759 --> 00:31:38,919
He's awesome!

618
00:31:38,920 --> 00:31:39,920
Stop talking.

619
00:31:48,079 --> 00:31:49,039
Just get him out of here!

620
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:50,720
You're the man, Boss P'Eng!

621
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:52,279
I love you!

622
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:54,839
Your friend is out of his mind.

623
00:31:55,039 --> 00:31:56,439
Just kissing people out of nowhere.

624
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:03,399
Why are you staring at me

625
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:04,520
with that look on your face?

626
00:32:06,279 --> 00:32:07,920
How can you even ask me that?

627
00:32:08,599 --> 00:32:09,640
What do you mean?

628
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:13,078
Don't you go around kissing
people for no reason too?

629
00:32:13,079 --> 00:32:14,079
You're one to talk.

630
00:32:37,279 --> 00:32:38,359
That's different.

631
00:32:40,519 --> 00:32:41,799
How is it different?

632
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:43,440
It's just...

633
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:47,960
P'Tao!

634
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:50,798
We just dug up a bottle from the dirt!

635
00:32:50,799 --> 00:32:52,119
What is this?

636
00:33:07,079 --> 00:33:08,199
What's this drawing of?

637
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,200
It's nothing.

638
00:33:09,279 --> 00:33:10,399
Just a drawing from when I was a kid.

639
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:12,240
I don't even remember
when it was buried here.

640
00:33:33,519 --> 00:33:34,680
Here we are.

641
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,200
All right.

642
00:33:48,799 --> 00:33:50,319
You're a real troublemaker.

643
00:33:50,559 --> 00:33:52,240
Boss P'Eng is such a germaphobe,

644
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:53,758
and you actually kissed him.

645
00:33:53,759 --> 00:33:54,920
You've got some nerve.

646
00:33:55,079 --> 00:33:56,079
You're so bad.

647
00:33:57,599 --> 00:34:00,440
I was just messing around
because I see him as a friend.

648
00:34:03,519 --> 00:34:05,200
So you kiss people just to mess with them?

649
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,518
You see me as a friend,

650
00:34:08,519 --> 00:34:09,800
and you've never kissed me.

651
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:13,360
Haven't I?

652
00:34:14,119 --> 00:34:15,119
Nope.

653
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:22,039
So by your logic,

654
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:24,119
you don't consider me a friend.

655
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,920
Well, do you consider me a friend?

656
00:34:30,039 --> 00:34:31,440
Only if you see me as a friend

657
00:34:31,719 --> 00:34:33,079
can I see you as one.

658
00:34:51,719 --> 00:34:53,480
Then what does it take to be your friend?

659
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:05,400
Give me a kiss,

660
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:07,039
and I'll tell you.

661
00:35:27,119 --> 00:35:28,719
If it's that easy to be your friend,

662
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,840
that's kind of boring.

663
00:35:32,199 --> 00:35:33,440
No fun at all.

664
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:42,239
Want a challenge?

665
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:47,679
Come here, I'll tell you.

666
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:56,199
Sleep with me.

667
00:36:38,239 --> 00:36:39,239
Here's your drink.

668
00:36:40,719 --> 00:36:42,400
Come have a drink.

669
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:47,399
I can't really handle
hard liquor like this.

670
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,920
Didn't you say you wanted to thank me?

671
00:36:59,719 --> 00:37:01,559
How can anyone actually enjoy

672
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:03,320
drinking this stuff?

673
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:05,078
Tastes like medicine.

674
00:37:05,079 --> 00:37:06,760
This is top-shelf liquor.

675
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:08,280
Sip it slowly,

676
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:09,480
you'll get used to it.

677
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:13,999
If I drink any more, I
won't be able to leave.

678
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,760
It wouldn't be your
first time staying over.

679
00:37:16,159 --> 00:37:17,360
Just stay.

680
00:37:21,079 --> 00:37:22,880
I have to take the kids home later.

681
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,760
It's too much trouble
having them stay here.

682
00:37:35,840 --> 00:37:37,760
Let Xiaotong and Xiaoya stay here.

683
00:37:38,039 --> 00:37:39,239
There are plenty of rooms.

684
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:40,920
You should move in too.

685
00:37:41,559 --> 00:37:43,919
I'll have the driver take them
to and from school every day.

686
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:44,920
It's very convenient.

687
00:37:47,119 --> 00:37:48,479
Are you drunk already
after just that little bit?

688
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:49,920
What nonsense are you talking about?

689
00:37:50,599 --> 00:37:52,960
How could I possibly let
them live in a mansion like this?

690
00:37:53,159 --> 00:37:54,519
What's wrong with a big house?

691
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,440
Isn't a big house nice?

692
00:37:57,119 --> 00:37:58,119
No, it's not.

693
00:37:58,719 --> 00:38:00,159
Once they get used to it,

694
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:03,135
they won't be able to
go back to a small place.

695
00:38:03,159 --> 00:38:05,119
I wouldn't get used to it,

696
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,519
and I wouldn't be able to leave.

697
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:10,119
Then don't leave.

698
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:24,920
I still want to find my
mom as soon as possible

699
00:38:25,639 --> 00:38:27,360
and return the ring to you.

700
00:38:27,679 --> 00:38:28,960
I don't want to owe you.

701
00:38:31,199 --> 00:38:33,800
I feel like I already owe you way too much.

702
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,719
You really do need to find your mom soon.

703
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:38,639
That ring means a great deal to me.

704
00:38:39,159 --> 00:38:40,559
If your family is short on cash,

705
00:38:41,440 --> 00:38:42,800
I can lend you some for now.

706
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:50,400
I want to find her as soon as I can, too.

707
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:52,880
Honestly, right now,

708
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:54,920
I really don't have any leads.

709
00:38:56,079 --> 00:38:57,719
All I can do is ask around

710
00:38:58,559 --> 00:38:59,800
and wait for news.

711
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,840
Do whatever it takes
to get in touch with her.

712
00:39:02,119 --> 00:39:03,119
Just tell her

713
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,840
money isn't an issue, I can handle it.

714
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:06,200
Tell her to come back right away.

715
00:39:15,559 --> 00:39:16,559
I...

716
00:39:18,559 --> 00:39:21,440
I can't let you keep paying
for my family's mistakes.

717
00:39:26,039 --> 00:39:27,199
What if...

718
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:34,920
I'm willing to pay the
price for my own feelings?

719
00:39:51,119 --> 00:39:52,400
What's going on?

720
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:56,199
My face didn't even burn
this much when he kissed me.

721
00:39:57,400 --> 00:39:59,119
How could just one sentence make me...

722
00:40:09,679 --> 00:40:10,960
This liquor

723
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:13,440
really packs a punch.

724
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:17,480
Since when am I such a lightweight?

725
00:40:17,719 --> 00:40:19,199
I'm so dizzy.

726
00:40:20,199 --> 00:40:21,360
There's a little bit left.

727
00:40:22,199 --> 00:40:23,199
Finish it up.

728
00:40:23,440 --> 00:40:25,360
Once you finish, I'll take you somewhere.

729
00:40:37,719 --> 00:40:38,719
Where?

730
00:40:40,239 --> 00:40:41,559
I'm taking you to a place

731
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:44,119
you've always been curious about.
